736752", "personaname": "aruvin", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/aruvin/", "num_games_owned": 666, "num_reviews": 167, "playtime_forever": 2417, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2781, "last_played": 1487426048, "avatar": "d15fdc3da233d258dc3a564da8199093f6a93d64"}, "language": "english", "review": "One of the classics that I would easily label as a \"no nonesense\" hardcore product that actually promotes co-op due to it's endless spawn of horde and perma-death feature. Those that are able to understand Alien Swarm's mechanic will play on a whole new level leaving some of us to watch in awe. It is an \"art\" to master to survive - in order to survive the hardest difficulty with endless onslaughts of aliens. \n\nThe campaign is rather short [b]but[/b] each map is intense and messy. It can be overwhelming for new players - until they get the hang of the gameplay/learn from the other players. There is a somewhat learning curve for players to understand each map's objective and how to handle them. \n\nNo nonesense fetching rubbish quest/picking up weapons/special loot. Go in, get the job done and get out alive. ASAP. Linger a few more seconds long and you might get swarmed. As it is 8 years old, playerbase in steam may be limited however in other community servers, there are still people playing it. \n\nThis is one of the few timeless jewel in STEAM. In my books, Alien Swarm easily nets a whopping 8/10. \n\nedit#1: Typo tag", "timestamp_created": 1532720652, "timestamp_updated": 1532720716, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.52173912525177002", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1279569600", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "43726645", "author": {"steamid": "76561198024583182", "personaname": "MaddMaddox", "persona_sta